{
  "version": 1,
  "canonicalRoot": "tools/schema-sync/typespec",
  "handMirrorDocs": "Hand mirror entries verify that hand-maintained native/TS schema copies still carry every field the generated canon defines (field name + optionality). check-hand-mirror.mjs loops every domain below. Each mirror entry may be a bare path string or an object { path, interfaces?, knownDrift? }. `interfaces` pins which generated interfaces the mirror must carry; omit it to auto-detect (TS mirrors: every generated interface the mirror file re-declares as `export interface`; native mirrors: every generated interface in the domain). `knownDrift` grandfathers the pre-existing divergences the checker enumerates — each token is `Interface.field` for a field present in generated output but absent from the mirror, or `Interface.field#opt` for an optionality mismatch (TS and C# mirrors). The gate FAILS closed when live drift exceeds the listed set (new drift) AND when a listed token is no longer real drift (stale grandfather), so the list ratchets down as the TypeSpec strangler migration burns it off. functions/src/types/legacy.ts is registered as a `tsHandMirror` so the doc types it re-declares a second time are field-checked against the canon; do NOT converge it by editing legacy.ts in this gate — burn the list down domain-at-a-time.",
